---

## 7. Non-conclusions

- The selected transverse contacts need not form a matching.
- A selected edge can be selected from both endpoints; the factor two is not removed.
- Selected contacts may belong to strict-rhombus trains, exceptional-face boundaries, or bridges as physical edges; the theorem only removes bridge payment for missing branching contacts.
- No individual KKT coefficient floor is proved.
- No source-preserving diameter-decreasing motion is constructed.

The result narrows the live problem to occupancy of more than `0.640D` transverse contacts in the stopped-train/exceptional-face network.

**Final verdict:** PASS at proof-only scope. C-II remains open.